libbtbb (2020-12-R1+fork1) unstable; urgency=low
  * Builds and installs out of the box on current tools: the CMake minimum is
    now 3.5, so CMake 4 accepts the project, and the Python tools get a PEP 440
    version and install from a wheel instead of the removed
    "setup.py install". Building them no longer has to be turned off.
  * Fixed undefined behaviour in the LE decoder and packet dump, and an
    unaligned, host-endian read of 16-bit service UUIDs in advertising data.

